Language English
Debug Off

Book PlaceDiningRoom Ordered No Keep Looped
	
	Page Locked
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @ExploreHall1ViaDiningRoomBlocked
		
		Prolog """
			The door is filthy, though the push plate is shiny, like it has
			been used recently.
		"""
		Button "Explore"
		
		Text """
			It's locked. You'll probably need a key to open it.
		"""
		
		Mark Unread
		Exit
	End Page Locked

	Page OpenDoor
		Triggered By @TalkedToBackyardBen If talkedToBenCount >= 2
		
		Add TileDiningRoom, TokenBackyardBenPassive, TokenDoorDiningRoom!
		Remove TokenExploreDiningRoomViaBackdoor, TokenBackyardBenBefore

		Text """
			<<Ah! Here's the key,>> Benjamin exclaims. He steps up to the door
			and unlocks it. A surprising amount of dirt falls as he pushes it
			open.

			The door creaks open and you see what looks like the servants'
			dining room. The room makes the yard look orderly. Heaps of rubbish
			and broken glassware are strewn about the room.

			Place the {c:TileDiningRoom} tile and door as indicated, then
			discard this Explore token.
		"""
		
		exploredDiningRoom = true
		
		// we want a clear event name for the name of the target investigator,
		// not some wacky constructed name
		// we raise an event to have EventChosenInvestigator assigned
		Trigger @ChooseInvestigator
	End Page OpenDoor
	
	Page Kitchen
		Add TokenExploreKitchenViaDiningRoom!
		
		Text """
			To the right, a doorway opens to the kitchen. Place an Explore token
			as indicated.
		"""
		
	End Page Kitchen

	Page OtherExplores
		Add TokenExploreBasementViaDiningRoomBlocked!, TokenExploreHall1ViaDiningRoomBlocked!

		Text """
			Two other doors lead farther into the house. Place Explore tokens
			as indicated.
		"""
	End Page OtherExplores
	
	Page FluxStabilizer
		Add TokenSearchDiningRoomFluxStabilizer!

		Text """
			An odd-looking device sits on the table. Place a Search token as
			indicated.
		"""
	End Page FluxStabilizer
	
	Page Paper
		Add TokenSearchDiningRoomPaper!
		
		Text """
			There's a box in the corner that was packed carelessly. Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		// we do this because if they haven't found the journal,
		// there will be another page after this one
		If foundJournal Then Trigger @MoveAfterExplore
	End Page Paper
	
	Page Journal
		Visible If Not foundJournal
		
		Text """
			As you walk into the house, you remember the book in the driveway
			and glance back toward the gate as you step inside. 
			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} moves 1 space into the explored area.
		"""
	End Page Journal
End Book PlaceDiningRoom

Book SearchDiningRoom Ordered No Keep Looped

	Page StartFluxStabilizer
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchDiningRoomFluxStabilizer If Unread
		If testMode Then Trigger @AskAboutGate
	
		Prolog "A small device with gears, hoses, and lights sits on the table."
		Button "Search"
	
		Text """
			As you reach down to pick it up, the device sparks and booms,
			generating a pressure wave that pushes all
			investigators--including you--1 space away from the
			device.

			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} recovers first and stands back up. 
			They approach the device but nothing happens. Move
			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} into the device's space.
		"""
		
		// wanderers are the cultists who seem to be coming from the secret
		// passageway off the study.
		wandererMax = #heros - exploredBackyardNicely
		If wandererMax < 1 Then wandererMax = 1
	End Page StartFluxStabilizer
	
	Page Finn
		Visible If #HeroFinnEdwards
		
		Text """
			Finn Edwards starts to come to, not sure at first where he is:  he
			is on the ground where he fell. As his vision clears, he feels
			different. He feels... off. Finn can no longer use his special
			ability.

			As he starts to push himself up, he puts his hand down in the wrong
			place. Hard. Pain. When he looks at what he hit, he gains the
			{c:QItemBrassKnuckles} Common Item. As he plays with them, they make
			him feel more confident. Improve Finn's {strength}.
		"""
	End Page Finn
	
	Page Kate
		Visible If #HeroKateWinthrop
		
		Text "Will Kate pick up the {c:QItemFluxStabilizer}?"
		
		Test "Yes" Or "No" Set katePicksUp
		If katePicksUp Then Goto KatePicksUp
		Goto KateDoesNotPickUp
	End Page Kate

	Page KatePicksUp
		Not Visible
		Text """
			Kate is overjoyed that she will have a {c:QItemFluxStablizer} again,
			especially one this powerful.
			
			Looking at it, she calms down and loses her focusing anger. Kate no
			longer becomes Focused when she is attacked.
			
			Kate says to the others, <<This device can repel monsters. I don't
			expect I'll need it here, but mine broke this morning
			and I didn't know how I'd find another.>>
		"""
		
		kateHasFluxStabilizer = true
		Goto Puzzle1
	End Page KatePicksUp
	
	Page KateDoesNotPickUp
		Not Visible
		Text """
			Kate quietly seethes to herself at the unfairness:  <i>That
			thing should be mine.</i>
			
			Kate becomes Focused.
		"""
		
		kateHasFluxStabilizer = false
		Goto Puzzle1
	End Page KateDoesNotPickUp

	Page Puzzle1
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchDiningRoomFluxStabilizer If Unread And StartFluxStabilizer Is Read

		Prolog """
			There is a control panel. You probably shouldn't, but maybe you can
			restart it? You reach down and begin to fiddle with the buttons and
			dials.

			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} may attempt the puzzle using {lore}.
		"""
		Button "Attempt puzzle"
		
		No Text
		
		Trigger @AttemptFluxStabilizerPuzzle
		If puzzleFluxStabilizerSolved Then Goto GetFluxStabilizer
		Goto DontGetFluxStabilizer
	End Page Puzzle1

	Page Puzzle2
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchDiningRoomFluxStabilizer If Puzzle1 Is Read
		
		Prolog """
			Maybe if you randomly flipped a few more buttons or turned a few
			more dials, it will do something.
			
			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} can attempt it again using {lore}.
		"""
		
		No Text
		
		Trigger @AttemptFluxStabilizerPuzzle
		If puzzleFluxStabilizerSolved Then Goto GetFluxStabilizer

		Mark Unread
		Goto DontGetFluxStabilizer
	End Page Puzzle2

	Page DontGetFluxStabilizer
		Not Visible
		Text """
			It still just sits there. Doing nothing. The hoses aren't moving,
			the lights are off, and it makes no noise.
		"""
		Exit
	End Page DontGetFluxStabilizer

	Page GetFluxStabilizer
		Not Visible
		
		Text QItemFluxStabilizer """
			The device sputters, then begins humming quietly.

			Gain the {c:QItemFluxStabilizer} common item, then discard
			this Search token.

			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} can drop or pick up this item. No other
			investigator can hold it. When the
			{c:QItemFluxStabilizer} is on the floor, any investigator who moves
			or is moved into its space immediately moves 1 space away from the
			device. Move toward the {c:TileDiningRoom} if possible; you do not
			evade monsters when moving this way.
			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} is immune to this effect.

			When {c:EventChosenInvestigator} holds this item, add 1 additional
			movement to their move actions.

			This information can be reviewed in the app.
		"""

		Remove TokenSearchDiningRoomFluxStabilizer
		Goto GetFluxStabilizer2
	End Page GetFluxStabilizer

	Page GetFluxStabilizer2
		Not Visible
		
		Add TokenDiningRoomBen!
		Remove TokenBackyardBenPassive
	
		Text """
			Benjamin walks through the door into the {c:TileDiningRoom}. Move
			the Purple Man token as indicated.

			As he walks in he says, <<I heard a noise. This house
			can be dangerous with everything in disarray. Please be careful.>>

			He seems to be holding something in his hand.
		"""
		
		If Not exploredBackyardNicely Then Text """
			Benjamin walks briskly through the door snapping, <<What are you
			folks doing in here?!>> Move the Purple Man token as indicated.

			He seems to have something in his hand.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page GetFluxStabilizer2

	Page PaperInBox
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchDiningRoomPaper
		
		Prolog "There's a yellowed scrap of paper in the box."
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenSearchDiningRoomPaper

		Text QItemEvidenceDiningRoom """
			The paper is old, yellowed, and dry. When you pick it up, a corner
			breaks off. The writing is faded but you can make out a few phrases.

			<<... this Saturday, the children will...>>

			<<... everything is ready, but my daughter doesn't know...>>

			<<Blood will... chapel... altar>>

			Gain the {c:QItemEvidenceDiningRoom} Unique Item and gain 2 {clue},
			then discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		foundEvidenceCount = foundEvidenceCount + 1
		Exit
	End Page PaperInBox
	
	Page ExploreHall1Blocked
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @ExploreHall1ViaDiningRoomBlocked
		
		Prolog """
			For an inside door, this one seems solid and imposing.
		"""
		Button "Explore"
		
		Text """
			It's locked. Maybe Ben has the key?
		"""
		
		Mark Unread
		Exit
	End Page ExploreHall1Blocked
End Book SearchDiningRoom

Book Kitchen Ordered No Keep Looped
	Page Explore
		Triggered By @ExploreKitchenViaDiningRoom
		
		Prolog """
			The swinging door doesn't look like it will hold up to much use, so
			you'll need to be careful.
		"""
		Button "Explore"

		Text """
			Compared to the dining room, the kitchen looks clean. The
			cupboards are empty. A couple of barrels of ale and a half-packed
			box are the on the floor. Several cooking tools were left 
			on the counter.
			
			<i>Maybe the rest of the house will be as easy to clean as this
			room,</i> you think. And you really hope it is:  your friend is
			paying you for the job, not by the hour.

			Discard this Explore token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenExploreKitchenViaDiningRoom
		
		exploredKitchen = true
		$MythosKitchen = true
	End Page Explore
	
	Page Cutlery
		
		Add TokenSearchKitchenCutlery!

		Text """
			A few pieces of cutlery have been left on the
			counter; place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
	End Page Cutlery
	
	Page Box
		Add TokenSearchKitchenRandom!

		Text """
			Next to you is a box that looks like it was filled in a
			hurry. Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Trigger @MoveAfterExplore
		Exit
	End Page Box
	
	Page SearchCutlery
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchKitchenCutlery
		
		Prolog """
			On closer inspection, the pile of cutlery is deep, like someone
			upended a drawer and then left.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Text QItemCutlery """
			Ouch! You cut yourself; take 1 facedown damage. While you watch,
			several drops of blood fall to the floor; take 1 horror ({will}
			negates).
			
			As you look up from where your blood landed, you notice something
			pushed under the counter. Gain the {c:QItemCutlery} Common Item,
			then discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenSearchKitchenCutlery
		
		Exit
	End Page SearchCutlery
	
	Page SearchRandom
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchKitchenRandom
		
		Prolog """
			A hastily-packed box of kitchen tools sits off to the side of the
			room near the door.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Text """
			You dig down, looking through the box. There are a number of
			bottles. One of them is half full and has an odd greenish glow.
			Gain an Elixir, then discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenSearchKitchenRandom
		
		Exit
	End Page SearchRandom
End Book Kitchen

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Book DoorBasementViaDiningRoomBlocked Ordered No Keep Looped
	// we check unlocked to make sure it has a value (it doesn't until it comes through
	// here at least once
	Triggered By @ExploreBasementViaDiningRoom If basementPhase <> unlocked
	
	// startup values are defined in Startup

	Page FirstStart
		Text """
			This door has a rusty lock. You can (maybe) think of a couple of
			ways to get through it. <i>But how to proceed?</i>
		"""
		Button 1, "{action} Use Brawn"
		Button 2, "{action} Use Brains"
		Button 3, "Cancel"
		
		If selection = 3 Then Exit
		basementSkill = brains
		If selection = 1 Then basementSkill = brawn
	End Page FirstStart

	Page FirstBrawn
		Visible If basementPhase = first And basementSkill = brawn
		
		Text """
			After struggling with the lock for several minutes, you lose your
			temper and hit it as hard as you can. Frustrated and in pain, you
			lean back and slide down to sit on the floor with your back against
			the door. You fume for a while and then it occurs to you! All you
			have to do is... ({lore}).
		"""
		Test "Pass" OR "Fail" Set basementUnlocked
	End Page FirstBrawn
	
	Page FirstBrawnPass
		Visible If basementPhase = first And basementSkill = brawn And basementUnlocked
	
		Text """
			Eureka! You figured it out. (You’ll wonder how that happened for a
			long time.) The house is dank and scary, but it’s just an old house.
			This isn’t so bad.

			Improve {lore} or {will}, then remove this Explore token.
		"""
		
		basementPhase = unlocked
	End Page FirstBrawnPass
	
	Page FirstBrawnFail
		Visible If basementPhase = first And basementSkill = brawn And Not basementUnlocked

		Text """
			<i>Well, what did I think would happen?!</i> you mutter to yourself.
			Frustrated, you swear never to think again.
		"""
		
		basementPhase = second
		basementSkill = none
	End Page FirstBrawnFail
	
	Page FirstBrains
		Visible If basementPhase = first And basementSkill = brains
		
		Text """
			After trying everything you can think of, you lose your temper and
			start to hit and kick the lock ({strength}).
		"""
		Test "Pass" OR "Fail" Set basementUnlocked
	End Page FirstBrains
	
	Page FirstBrainsPass
		Visible If basementPhase = first And basementSkill = brains And basementUnlocked
	
		Text """
			<<I didn’t know I had it in me!>> you exclaim. Improve {strength} or
			{will}, then discard this Explore token.
		"""
		
		basementPhase = unlocked
	End Page FirstBrainsPass
	
	Page FirstBrainsFail
		Visible If basementPhase = first And basementSkill = brains And Not basementUnlocked

		Text """
			Feeling like you can’t do anything right, you settle into a sulk.
			<i>I really need to watch my temper today,</i> you think. You hand
			is still throbbing with pain. Take 1 Damage ({will}).
		"""
		
		basementPhase = second
		basementSkill = none
	End Page FirstBrainsFail

	Page SecondStart
		Visible If basementPhase = second
		
		Text """
			The lock resists your attempts to release it. You'll need to try
			again.
		"""
		Button 1, "{action} Use Brawn"
		Button 2, "{action} Use Brains"
		Button 3, "Cancel"
		
		If selection = 3 Then Exit
		basementSkill = brains
		If selection = 1 Then basementSkill = brawn
	End Page SecondStart

	Page SecondBrawn
		Visible If basementPhase = second And basementSkill = brawn
		
		Text """
			Refreshed from your break, you try again ({strength}). You grab the
			handle and prepare to pull as hard as you can.
		"""
		Test "Pass" OR "Fail" Set basementUnlocked
	End Page SecondBrawn
	
	Page SecondBrawnPass
		Visible If basementPhase = second And basementSkill = brawn And basementUnlocked
	
		Text """
			Your hand hurts almost as much as your pride, but at least it's
			unlocked. Discard this Explore token.
		"""
		
		basementPhase = unlocked
	End Page SecondBrawnPass
	
	Page SecondBrawnFail
		Visible If basementPhase = second And basementSkill = brawn And Not basementUnlocked

		Text """
			Your hand hurts from the effort and your frustration mounts. The 
			handle might be bent a little. <i>Best not to mention this,</i> you
			convince yourself.
		"""
		
		basementPhase = third
		basementSkill = none
	End Page SecondBrawnFail
	
	Page SecondBrains
		Visible If basementPhase = second And basementSkill = brains
		
		Text """
			Out of breath, you rest for a minute, then try again ({lore}).
			You lean down to look at the lock and consider your options.
		"""
		Test "Pass" OR "Fail" Set basementUnlocked
	End Page SecondBrains
	
	Page SecondBrainsPass
		Visible If basementPhase = second And basementSkill = brains And basementUnlocked
	
		Text """
			<i>That took longer than I expected,</i>n you think. You're
			embarrassed that you couldn't do it faster, but you feel better now
			that it's unlocked.
		"""
		
		basementPhase = unlocked
	End Page SecondBrainsPass
	
	Page SecondBrainsFail
		Visible If basementPhase = second And basementSkill = brains And Not basementUnlocked

		Text """
			<<What's wrong with me today?</i> you ask yourself. The other 
			investigators look at you oddly and you realize you said that out
			loud.
			
			Take 1 Horror ({will} negates)
		"""
		
		basementPhase = third
		basementSkill = none
	End Page SecondBrainsFail
	
	Page ThirdStart
		Visible If basementPhase = third
		Text """
			...
		"""
		Button 1, "{action} Use Brawn"
		Button 2, "{action} Use Brains"
		Button 3, "Cancel"
		
		If selection = 3 Then Exit
		basementSkill = brains
		If selection = 1 Then basementSkill = brawn
	End Page ThirdStart

	Page ThirdBrawn
		Visible If basementPhase = third And basementSkill = brawn
		
		Text """
			({strength}).
		"""
		Test "Pass" OR "Fail" Set basementUnlocked
	End Page ThirdBrawn
	
	Page ThirdBrawnPass
		Visible If basementPhase = third And basementSkill = brawn And basementUnlocked
	
		Text """
			The lock finally gives way but you've hurt your hand even more from
			the effort. Take 1 Damage and remove this Explore token.
		"""
		
		basementPhase = unlocked
	End Page ThirdBrawnPass
	
	Page ThirdBrawnFail
		Visible If basementPhase = third And basementSkill = brawn And Not basementUnlocked

		Text """
			((sigh))
		"""
		
		basementPhase = third
		basementSkill = none
		Mark Unread
		Mark ThirdBrawn Unread
		Mark ThirdStart Unread
	End Page ThirdBrawnFail
	
	Page ThirdBrains
		Visible If basementPhase = third And basementSkill = brains
		
		Text """
			({lore}).
		"""
		Test "Pass" OR "Fail" Set basementUnlocked
	End Page ThirdBrains
	
	Page ThirdBrainsPass
		Visible If basementPhase = third And basementSkill = brains And basementUnlocked
	
		Text """
			Though you finally figured it out, taking so long has shaken your
			confidence and made you wonder how smart you really are. Take 1
			facedown Horror, then remove this Explore token.
		"""
		
		basementPhase = unlocked
	End Page ThirdBrainsPass
	
	Page ThirdBrainsFail
		Visible If basementPhase = third And basementSkill = brains And Not basementUnlocked

		Text """
			...!
		"""
		
		basementPhase = third
		basementSkill = none
		Mark Unread
		Mark ThirdBrains Unread
		Mark ThirdStart Unread
	End Page ThirdBrainsFail	


	Page Unlocked
		Visible If basementPhase = unlocked
		
		Remove TokenExploreBasementViaDiningRoomBlocked
		Add TokenDarknessDiningRoom1!
		Add TokenDarknessDiningRoom2!
		Add TokenExploreBasementViaDiningRoom!
		
		Text """
			Now that the lock is loose, you open the door. The darkness
			seems to bleed into the room. You thought the dining room was dark
			when you first walked in, but now you know it was merely dim. Place
			darkness in each space of the dining room.

			When you try to look through the door into the basement, your vision
			is blocked by a darkness that almost feels solid. An investigator
			with a light source may enter the basement. Place a Sight token as
			indicated.
		"""
	End Page
End Book DoorBasementViaDiningRoomBlocked


